    "llm_raw_response": "<response>\n  <verdict>Existing</verdict>\n  <justification>One human whole-genome sequencing study of a familial ASD cohort (PMID: 35190550) identified putative disease-causing noncoding variants within brain-specific promoters/enhancers for ACTG1, listing it among known ASD and neurodevelopmental disease genes. This represents a credible human genetic association, though it is limited (a single cohort study with regulatory variant annotation rather than replicated causal validation). Other articles link ACTG1 to Baraitser-Winter syndrome, hearing loss, and neurodevelopmental phenotypes, with some cases mentioning possible autism features (PMID: 28496999), supporting a neurodevelopmental connection. However, the evidence specifically for ASD causation is not definitive or widely replicated, placing this in the Existing category rather than Established.</justification>\n  <pmids>\n    <pmid>35190550</pmid>\n    <pmid>28496999</pmid>\n    <pmid>31171384</pmid>\n  </pmids>\n</response>",
